// Cross-topic consolidation for Unit 2 topics 3.2.4 and 3.2.5 (Phase 4 Batch 2, owned by the cluster author).
// Chain: HIV structure → replication in CD4 helper T cells → antigens and recognition → B-cell response and antibodies →
// primary and secondary responses → vaccination and disease prevention.
// Scope follows PHASE4_BATCH2_MANIFEST.md: helper T cells "initiate the body's response" (3.2.4.2); antigen destruction is
// limited to agglutination and phagocytosis of bacterial cells (no neutralisation, complement or opsonin terminology);
// the fall in helper T cells in untreated HIV infection, AIDS, opportunistic infections, latency and clonal selection
// are labelled "(supporting)"; drug names are not required, so drugs are described by target in the question.
// Herd immunity is a concept only: no single universal threshold is given. Language follows the manifest: people living
// with HIV, no blame framing. Nothing here is medical advice.
// Question ids q-cl24-… and card ids f-cl24-… are unique site-wide. Data are either labelled hypothetical or cited.
